Stronger conceptual formulation

Autonomically Perpetuated Clerical Deprivation

An institutional condition in which administrative mechanisms, whether through negligence, defective procedures, deliberate conduct, or inadequate oversight, independently perpetuate the denial of documentary access, procedural participation, or institutional entitlements.

Important distinction: 
The phrase is a proposed conceptual classification, not an established legal doctrine. Establishing unlawful deprivation requires identifying the applicable legal entitlement, responsible authority, specific conduct, evidence, and resulting harm.
